X-CLIENT decision point (2026-05-29, ~53 CI cycles). The X SERVER serves in-page under blink (witnessed) + the client CONNECT works (FindListenerByPath). The remaining X-client-render needs cooperative multitasking of 2 blink VMs through BLOCKING syscalls -- a fundamental wall: making poll/epoll/select non-blocking (returning 0/EAGAIN) breaks the clients X handshake read (returns EOF instantly -> unable to open display); making them block freezes the other VM. The CORRECT fix is YIELD-AND-RETRY: on would-block, suspend the VM (preempt) + run the other VM + resume + retry when ready. Two viable architectures: (A) blink coroutine syscalls -- poll/read/epoll_wait/select that yield to the scheduler instead of block/return-EAGAIN (substantial blink-core change, single thread); (B) dual web workers + shared SAB memory -- server in worker A, client in worker B, each with its own runtime/runway, AF_UNIX socketpair (real host fds) or SAB ring bridges them; matches the existing worker-scheduling PRD and avoids fighting the single-thread scheduler. RECOMMEND (B) -- more robust, reuses the -pthread shared-memory build, gives each VM real concurrency. Pushed: blink 6c460d2 (non-blocking poll/select/epoll -- partial, to be superseded by yield model), webix Xvfb-patched+server.xkm+runConcurrent. Headline achieved+witnessed: a REAL X server runs+serves in-page under blink/WASM, no external services.